      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5dfe799f8ac300528b0212f4|full_name}:\nIt is caused by the scale of the headbone being set to 0 if your viewpoint is \"close\" to it(you can see the distance if fix your avatar's position with an animation, and then walk away from your avatar in vr)\nHowever, there should still be a way to toggle that off for specific avatars. (E.g. if that avatar's entire visible body is attached to its headbone[you can circumvent this somewhat by making a proxy headbone and using position and rotation constraints to force it to follow the headbone, but that worsens performance for everyone, to fix an issue only the wearer will have])",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
